---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const checks = [
  ["install", "Dependencies install"],
  ["build", "Project builds"],
  ["boot", "Server answers"],
  ["page load", "Entry page loads"],
  ["visible content", "Something meaningful renders"],
  ["application errors", "No uncaught or console error"],
  ["resource loads", "Same-origin assets load"],
  ["server errors", "No observed 5xx response"],
  ["client secrets", "Complete same-origin responses contain no detected secret"],
  ["network egress", "External origins match the allowlist"],
];
---

<Base
  title="Docs Trials: Can an agent actually build from your docs?"
  description="Run a coding agent against your documentation, verify the application it builds, and keep evidence you can inspect."
>
  <section class="hero shell" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="pill-row">
        <span class="pill">Local CLI</span>
        <span class="pill pill-outline">Evidence before opinions</span>
      </p>
      <h1 id="hero-title">
        Can an agent actually build from <mark>your docs</mark>?
      </h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Give a coding agent your documentation and a disposable starter app. Docs Trials freezes the
        inputs, runs deterministic checks against what the agent builds, and writes a local report
        with evidence references.
      </p>

      <div class="install-card" role="region" aria-labelledby="install-card-title">
        <div class="install-card-bar">
          <h2 id="install-card-title">Install</h2>
          <span class="sticker sticker-amber">Pre-release</span>
        </div>
        <pre><code><span class="prompt" aria-hidden="true">$ </span>npm install -g docs-trials
<span class="prompt" aria-hidden="true">$ </span>docs-trials install-browser</code></pre>
        <p class="install-note">
          <strong>Not on npm yet.</strong> Publication is pending owner approval. After release, these
          commands install the CLI and its Chromium build. Node 22 or later on macOS or Linux.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button primary" href="/report/">Inspect a real report</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href="#install"
          >Release status <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a
        >
      </div>
      <ul class="hero-facts" aria-label="Product facts">
        <li>Runs on your machine</li>
        <li>No model grades itself</li>
        <li>No overall score</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="terminal-wrap" role="region" aria-label="Excerpt from a local Docs Trials report">
      <span class="sticker sticker-violet terminal-label">Observed, not inferred</span>
      <div class="terminal">
        <div class="terminal-bar">
          <span class="terminal-dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
          <span>AX.md</span>
          <span>real attempt</span>
        </div>
        <p class="terminal-status">BASELINE PASSED</p>
        <p class="terminal-warning">Task fulfillment was not verified.</p>
        <div class="terminal-rule"></div>
        <p><b>PASS</b> Dependencies install successfully.</p>
        <p><b>PASS</b> The application answers HTTP 200.</p>
        <p><b>PASS</b> The entry page renders visible text.</p>
        <p><b>PASS</b> No application console error occurs.</p>
        <p><b>PASS</b> External origins match the allowlist.</p>
        <div class="terminal-rule"></div>
        <p class="terminal-meta">9 passed · 0 failed · 0 inconclusive</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="proof-strip" aria-label="Product position">
    <p><span aria-hidden="true">≠</span> A successful build is not a working integration.</p>
    <p><span aria-hidden="true">≠</span> A browser observation is not proof of task completion.</p>
    <p>
      <span aria-hidden="true">≠</span> A failed check is not automatically a documentation finding.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="method shell section" id="method" aria-labelledby="method-title">
    <header class="section-heading">
      <p class="kicker">The method</p>
      <h2 id="method-title">One frozen trial. One real build. Evidence for every result.</h2>
    </header>
    <ol class="method-grid">
      <li class="tone-violet">
        <span class="step-number">01</span>
        <h3>Freeze the trial</h3>
        <p>
          Record the task, documentation snapshots, commands, allowlists, agent, and starter
          revision.
        </p>
        <code>docs-trials prepare</code>
      </li>
      <li class="tone-amber">
        <span class="step-number">02</span>
        <h3>Let the agent build</h3>
        <p>Give the generated instructions to your coding agent in a disposable workspace.</p>
        <code>AGENT_INSTRUCTIONS.md</code>
      </li>
      <li class="tone-lime">
        <span class="step-number">03</span>
        <h3>Verify the result</h3>
        <p>
          Install, build, boot, and observe the application in Chromium with deterministic checks.
        </p>
        <code>docs-trials verify latest</code>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="report-feature shell section" aria-labelledby="report-feature-title">
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">A report, not a score</p>
      <h2 id="report-feature-title">The local report links results to retained evidence.</h2>
      <p>
        The report names what ran, what the browser observed, what remained unresolved, and which
        author goals were not graded. Retained command and browser observations stay beside it.
      </p>
      <a class="inline-link" href="/report/"
        >Inspect the report and evidence <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a
      >
    </div>
    <dl class="report-ledger">
      <div><dt>Outcome</dt><dd class="pass-text">Baseline passed</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Checks</dt><dd>9 / 9 passed</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Agent</dt><dd>OpenCode · gpt-5.6-sol</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Evidence</dt><dd>Install · boot · browser · source diff</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Task goals</dt><dd>Recorded, not verified</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="checks section" id="checks" aria-labelledby="checks-title">
    <div class="shell checks-layout">
      <header class="section-heading sticky-heading">
        <p class="kicker">Deterministic baseline</p>
        <h2 id="checks-title">Ten checks. No model verdict.</h2>
        <p>
          Checks apply only when their lifecycle step exists. Missing evidence and infrastructure
          trouble are inconclusive, never silently passed.
        </p>
        <ul class="outcome-key" aria-label="Possible outcomes">
          <li class="key-pass">passed</li>
          <li class="key-fail">failed</li>
          <li class="key-inconclusive">inconclusive</li>
        </ul>
      </header>
      <ol class="check-list">
        {
          checks.map(([name, description], index) => (
            <li>
              <span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span>
              <strong>{name}</strong>
              <p>{description}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="limits shell section" aria-labelledby="limits-title">
    <div class="limits-title">
      <p class="kicker">The honesty clause</p>
      <h2 id="limits-title">What Docs Trials refuses to claim</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="limits-list">
      <article>
        <h3>“The task is complete.”</h3>
        <p>
          The baseline checks mechanical web health. Author goals remain visible and explicitly
          ungraded.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>“The docs caused this.”</h3>
        <p>
          A failed attempt becomes a documentation finding only after evidence supports that
          attribution.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>“This agent is better.”</h3>
        <p>One stochastic attempt is a diagnostic observation, not a benchmark or leaderboard.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>“Your machine is isolated.”</h3>
        <p>
          Commands run as your user. Use disposable workspaces and remove credentials before
          starting.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="install section" id="install" aria-labelledby="install-title">
    <div class="shell install-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker inverse">Pre-release</p>
        <h2 id="install-title">Installation is not public yet.</h2>
        <p>
          The inspectable public sample and operator guidance are complete. The npm package has not
          been published. Docs Trials sends no telemetry or reports, but project commands can make
          unrestricted network requests.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ol class="status-list" aria-label="Release status">
        <li class="status-done"><span>Done</span><code>Public sample complete</code></li>
        <li class="status-done"><span>Done</span><code>Operator skill complete</code></li>
        <li class="status-pending">
          <span>Pending</span><code>npm publication pending approval</code>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="closing shell section" aria-labelledby="closing-title">
    <p class="closing-mark" aria-hidden="true">DT / 00</p>
    <h2 id="closing-title">Test the documentation by building from it.</h2>
    <div>
      <p>
        Keep the inputs frozen. Keep the verdict deterministic. Keep every public claim
        reproducible.
      </p>
      <a class="button primary" href="https://github.com/AbdulsaboorS/docs-trials"
        >View the source</a
      >
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
